## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize to faster than O(n^2 k)?
- How to handle negatives or alternative cost such as max/min?

## Why This Is Asked
This problem introduces a dynamic programming angle where subarrays are weighted by their block index. It tests the ability to transform interval sums into prefix sums, derive a two-dimensional DP over position and block count, and implement solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) interval sum computation
- 2D DP over position and block count
- Solution reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time complexity: O(n²k); Space complexity: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScorePartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = [0];
  for (let x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1] + x);
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][1] = P[i];
  }

  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
        const score = dp[p][t-1] + (P[i] - P[p]) * t;
        if (score > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = score;
          parent[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct partitions
  const partitions = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = parent[end][t];
    partitions.unshift([start+1, end]);
    end = start;
  }

  return { maxScore: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests 1D partition DP, median-based block costs, and reconstruction; mirrors realistic facility placement.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions
- Median-based block cost
- Prefix sums for O(1) block cost
- Backpointer reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPostOffice(X, k) {
  const n = X.length;
  const cost = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));

  // Precompute prefix sums for O(1) range sum queries
  const prefix = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + X[i];
  }

  // Precompute block costs using median property
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      const m = Math.floor((l + r) / 2);
      cost[l][r] = (X[m] * (m - l) - (prefix[m] - prefix[l])) +
                   ((prefix[r + 1] - prefix[m + 1]) - X[m] * (r - m));
    }
  }

  // DP table and backpointers
  const dp = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let p = 1; p <= k; p++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = p - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const candidate = dp[j][p - 1] + cost[j][i - 1];
        if (candidate < dp[i][p]) {
          dp[i][p] = candidate;
          parent[i][p] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let curr = n;
  for (let p = k; p >= 1; p--) {
    const start = parent[curr][p];
    blocks.unshift([start, curr - 1]);
    curr = start;
  }

  return { cost: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Complexity Analysis
- Time: O(kn²) for DP transitions plus O(n²) for cost preprocessing
- Space: O(nk) for DP table, reducible to O(n) with layer optimization

